-- title:
--   Transport of a crossing-model presentation along a ring isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a commutative local ring, $\varpi_0 \in A_0$, $w \in \mathbb{N}$, and write $\hat A_0 =$ `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A₀) A₀` for the completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal. Let $R$ be a commutative local ring, $b : A_0 \to R$ a ring homomorphism, and let $e$ be a ring isomorphism from the maximal-adic completion $\hat R$ onto the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,\hat A_0\,\pi$, that is, onto $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,\hat A_0$ modulo the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\pi)$, where $\pi$ is the $w$-th power of the image of $\varpi_0$ in $\hat A_0$. Assume the compatibility $e(b(a)) = \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,(a)$ for all $a \in A_0$, where images in the completions are taken along the canonical maps and $\mathrm{const}\,\pi\,(x)$ denotes the class of the constant power series $C(x)$. Let $N$ be a commutative local ring and $\theta : R \xrightarrow{\sim} N$ a ring isomorphism. Then there exist a ring homomorphism $\sigma : \hat A_0 \to \hat N$ and a ring isomorphism $\iota : \hat N \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,\hat A_0\,\pi$ such that $\sigma$ carries the image of $a \in A_0$ in $\hat A_0$ to the image of $\theta(b(a))$ in $\hat N$; $\iota(\sigma(o)) = \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,(o)$ for every $o \in \hat A_0$; and $\iota$ applied to the image of $\theta(r)$ in $\hat N$ equals $e$ applied to the image of $r$ in $\hat R$, for every $r \in R$.
--
--   This is the transport step for formal crossing (ordinary double point) data: a presentation of the completed local ring $\hat R$ as $\hat A_0[[u,v]]/(uv-\varpi_0^w)$ over $\hat A_0$, compatible with the structure map coming from $b$, is carried along any isomorphism $R \cong N$ of local rings to a presentation of $\hat N$ with the same base data. It is used in the analysis of nodal points on modular curves, in particular by the node-ring coordinate statement and by the per-node conclusions at the primes $2$ and $3$ in the full-level Diamond argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_of_ringEquiv.lean

import Mathlib
